<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/TradingScheduleOverrideNotice/role/overrideForFacility> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "exact TradingFacility version whose sessions are overridden";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingScheduleOverrideNotice;
    rdfs:label "override facility";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingFacility.
fin-market-structure:TradingSessionOccurrence a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Trading Session Occurrence, is a dated scheduled session window materialized from one exact session template and calendar version for one exact facility version and represented as a UTC half-open interval, used to denote a concrete scheduled time window. Whether the window is effectively tradable is a derived result expressed by the optional effectiveSessionStartUtc and effectiveSessionEndUtc attributes after applying any TradingScheduleOverrideNotice facts; a window removed by a holiday or closure has no effective tradable interval rather than losing its scheduled identity.";
    rdfs:label "Trading Session Occurrence";
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r_3a1073bf6a41fe1c6453acf3, _:r_57fa0ebc4cbe5aecfff97edf, _:r_5ac2eaded6d4e9b4eb40be7d, _:r_634988deb3de88a1712e5acb, _:r_72330df6d2f784e8c348b9ef, _:r_755ab6e55b5331e277b332a3, _:r_776fd511a2620e3c6062cb76, _:r_7ef394d792029f013c4d057e, _:r_8cdb0fb72f688b04487fa5cf, _:r_8f6474361bb278a0e69ebd3b, _:r_a0a35e0c7f3430fd39c3413a, _:r_ba8f5306af92e4c59c5ba483, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/ProvenancedFact>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/TemporalFact>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/TradingSessionOccurrence/LogicalIdentity> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Stable FactIdentity companion for immutable Trading Session Occurrence versions.";
    rdfs:label "Trading Session Occurrence logical identity";
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactIdentity>;
    owl:disjointWith <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>.
fin-market-structure:TradingSessionTemplate a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Trading Session Template, is a local-clock recurring session specification attached to one exact TradingCalendar version, used to define repeatedly applicable session start, end, phase, and recurrence rules that deterministically materialize into UTC half-open occurrence intervals under the calendar's IANA time zone.";
    rdfs:label "Trading Session Template";
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r_07cac72630002fa3a9562545, _:r_13655d4c36487e0e84251165, _:r_4cdd1dca1a9322d979c93081, _:r_68a87c2d4bd6f9edd5b7334e, _:r_716ecd4e4ed3026ef2408521, _:r_8b34096376d617ab9779aed4, _:r_937c7615eff6b35daa06132b, _:r_94acff33a777d73265907822, _:r_99ed3bd3994bcc7397172ebc, _:r_d105b6101f77fb55c4674f5a, _:r_d443f551ef7ae1cce8e99a45, _:r_da69057a11751f3fe51e375b, _:r_daa5a6678cead372c25c0bcc, _:r_e3797db205f205e1e54b2190, _:r_edd5ce38b90549717f642597, _:r_f352ed8a95d8321363e7e1a3, _:r_f81318be6d249b38d4d221c9, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/ProvenancedFact>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/TemporalFact>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/TradingSessionTemplate/LogicalIdentity> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Stable FactIdentity companion for immutable Trading Session Template versions.";
    rdfs:label "Trading Session Template logical identity";
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactIdentity>;
    owl:disjointWith <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>.
fin-market-structure:TradingVenue a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Trading Venue, is a trading facility that constitutes, maintains, or provides a market system on which financial instruments may be admitted to trading, used to identify a market system or venue (a regulated market, multilateral trading facility, organized trading facility, or comparable trading platform) distinct from the legal entity that operates it. The operator and the regulatory category of the venue are modeled separately as temporal, evidenced facts via VenueOperation rather than as part of the venue identity.";
    rdfs:label "Trading Venue";
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r_01aa9e3fc7a8f4e86753dd39, _:r_52f329eed3c737c53f2d6205, _:r_7f462e7756857a675ae2f206, _:r_966d70881fb5b2da930913c8, _:r_96c6acc1f311e7c1de4c7aae, _:r_f685d12328c11fd9199a1e24, fin-market-structure:TradingFacility, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/ProvenancedFact>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/TemporalFact>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/TradingVenue/LogicalIdentity> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Stable FactIdentity companion for immutable Trading Venue versions.";
    rdfs:label "Trading Venue logical identity";
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactIdentity>;
    owl:disjointWith <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>.
fin-market-structure:VenueCategory a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Venue Category, is a closed controlled vocabulary of regulatory trading-venue categories, used to classify a TradingVenue as a temporal evidenced fact rather than a global supertree.";
    rdfs:label "Venue Category";
    owl:oneOf _:l_02119b585659c2c442d694a9_0.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/scheme> a skos:ConceptScheme;
    skos:prefLabel "Venue Category";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/value/multilateralTradingFacility> a owl:NamedIndividual, skos:Concept, fin-market-structure:VenueCategory;
    rdfs:comment "venue authorized as a multilateral trading facility (e.g. EU MTF)";
    skos:inScheme <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/scheme>;
    skos:notation "multilateralTradingFacility";
    skos:prefLabel "Multilateral Trading Facility";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/value/organizedTradingFacility> a owl:NamedIndividual, skos:Concept, fin-market-structure:VenueCategory;
    rdfs:comment "venue authorized as an organized trading facility (e.g. EU OTF)";
    skos:inScheme <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/scheme>;
    skos:notation "organizedTradingFacility";
    skos:prefLabel "Organized Trading Facility";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/value/otherTradingVenue> a owl:NamedIndividual, skos:Concept, fin-market-structure:VenueCategory;
    rdfs:comment "venue authorized under another comparable trading-venue regime (e.g. ATS, exchange)";
    skos:inScheme <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/scheme>;
    skos:notation "otherTradingVenue";
    skos:prefLabel "Other Trading Venue";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/value/regulatedMarket> a owl:NamedIndividual, skos:Concept, fin-market-structure:VenueCategory;
    rdfs:comment "venue authorized as a regulated market (e.g. EU RM)";
    skos:inScheme <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/scheme>;
    skos:notation "regulatedMarket";
    skos:prefLabel "Regulated Market";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
fin-market-structure:VenueOperation a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Venue Operation, is a temporal provenance-bearing association that records one logical Party operating one logical TradingVenue over a validity interval together with an optional regulatory venue category, used to separate the market system/venue from the legal entity that operates it and to model operator history without conflating venue identity with its operator.";
    rdfs:label "Venue Operation";
    rdfs:subClassOf _:r_059b878487b28f42936f437d, _:r_11ac137207295898c271958b, _:r_20f83b5b2e2a1306aa94cfe0, _:r_2c1043bff129c5f48374b2fd, _:r_426f9d5c61096de5a6b3c8d0, _:r_8304170d95417c43430e0507, _:r_98692dd89502df97f71748bc, _:r_9f7a194bdd387d8c79f65ae3, _:r_d71277d2bea7f3cc0d3a0b17, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/ProvenancedFact>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/patterns/TemporalFact>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueOperation/LogicalIdentity> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Stable FactIdentity companion for immutable Venue Operation versions.";
    rdfs:label "Venue Operation logical identity";
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactIdentity>;
    owl:disjointWith <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/data-binding/FactVersion>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueOperation/role/operatedVenue> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "logical TradingVenue identity operated by the party";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:VenueOperation;
    rdfs:label "operated venue";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingVenue.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueOperation/role/operatingParty> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "logical Party identity that operates the venue";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:VenueOperation;
    rdfs:label "operating party";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Party>.
fin-market-structure:authorityCalendarId a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Authority Calendar Identifier, is a non-empty NFC string identifier assigned to a trading calendar by its maintaining authority, used to uniquely denote that calendar within the scope of (authority, facility). The calendar logical key is the three-component (calendarFacility, calendarAuthority, authorityCalendarId) per TradingCalendarIdentityContract, so the identifier is unique within each authority-and-facility pair, not within the authority alone.";
    rdfs:label "Authority Calendar Identifier";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:authoritySessionId a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Authority Session Identifier, is a non-empty NFC string identifier assigned to a session template by its maintaining authority, used to uniquely denote that session within the authority-and-calendar scope.";
    rdfs:label "Authority Session Identifier";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:calendarAuthority a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Calendar Authority, is a functional relation that associates a trading calendar with the Party logical identity of its maintaining authority, used to characterize the institutional responsibility for the calendar.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingCalendar;
    rdfs:label "Calendar Authority";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Party/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:calendarExceptionKind a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Calendar Exception Kind, is a closed classification attribute of a calendar exception, used to distinguish holidays, closures, early closings, late openings, and similar exceptional circumstances.";
    rdfs:label "Calendar Exception Kind";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:CalendarExceptionKind.
fin-market-structure:calendarFacility a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Calendar Facility, is a functional relation that associates a trading calendar with the stable logical identity of its trading facility, used to characterize the venue that the calendar serves.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingCalendar;
    rdfs:label "Calendar Facility";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/TradingFacility/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:calendarJurisdiction a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Calendar Jurisdiction, is a functional relation that associates a trading calendar with its unique governing jurisdiction logical identity, used to characterize the regulatory and territorial attribution of the calendar.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingCalendar;
    rdfs:label "Calendar Jurisdiction";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Jurisdiction/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:componentOf a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Component Of, is a functional relation that associates a MarketInfrastructureComponent with the unique operating market infrastructure entity it is a section or component of, used to carry the ISO 10383 \"section\" part-of semantics independently of any facility supertype shared for reference range.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:MarketInfrastructureComponent;
    rdfs:label "Component Of";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/MICIdentifiedMarketInfrastructure/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:dstOverlapPolicy a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "DST Overlap Policy, is a closed classification attribute carried by a trading calendar, used to declare how local-clock instants that fall inside a DST gap or fold are interpreted during local-to-UTC materialization.";
    rdfs:label "DST Overlap Policy";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:DstOverlapPolicy.
fin-market-structure:effectiveSessionEndUtc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Effective Session End UTC, is an optional exclusive UTC instant at which a session occurrence stops being effectively tradable after applying any TradingScheduleOverrideNotice facts, used to separate the scheduled window from the effective tradable interval.";
    rdfs:label "Effective Session End UTC";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:effectiveSessionStartUtc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Effective Session Start UTC, is an optional inclusive UTC instant at which a session occurrence becomes effectively tradable after applying any TradingScheduleOverrideNotice facts, used to separate the scheduled window from the effective tradable interval. When absent and no cancellation applies, the effective interval equals the scheduled interval.";
    rdfs:label "Effective Session Start UTC";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:endDayOffset a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "End Day Offset, is a signed integer day offset between the local start date and the local end date of a session, used to model cross-midnight sessions where the end falls on a later calendar day than the start.";
    rdfs:label "End Day Offset";
    rdfs:range xsd:integer.
fin-market-structure:exceptionBusinessDate a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Exception Business Date, is the local business date on which a trading-calendar exception applies, used to attach an exception fact to a specific date.";
    rdfs:label "Exception Business Date";
    rdfs:range xsd:date.
fin-market-structure:exceptionOccurrence a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Exception Occurrence, is a functional relation that associates a calendar exception with the exact session occurrence it deterministically alters, used to attach an exception fact to the affected session occurrence.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingCalendarException;
    rdfs:label "Exception Occurrence";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingSessionOccurrence.
fin-market-structure:ianaTimeZone a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "IANA Time Zone, is a canonical IANA time-zone identifier, used to interpret the local-clock sessions of a trading calendar and anchor local sessions to a specific geographical time zone.";
    rdfs:label "IANA Time Zone";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:localSessionEnd a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Local Session End, is the ISO local-clock time at which a recurring half-open session interval ends, used to define the closing of a trading session in local time.";
    rdfs:label "Local Session End";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:localSessionStart a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Local Session Start, is the ISO local-clock time at which a recurring session interval begins, used to define the opening of a trading session in local time.";
    rdfs:label "Local Session Start";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:marketCategory a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "MIC Market Category, is a closed classification attribute carried by a MIC registry entry, used to record the ISO 10383 market category of the identified infrastructure.";
    rdfs:label "MIC Market Category";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:MICMarketCategory.
fin-market-structure:marketConvention a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Market Convention, is a reviewed convention member, used to fix the orientation and application semantics of one OTC context and characterize the pricing and unit orientation of over-the-counter quotes.";
    rdfs:label "Market Convention";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:MarketConvention.
fin-market-structure:marketSegmentVenue a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Market Segment Venue, is a functional relation that associates a market segment with the unique operating trading venue it belongs to, used to characterize the ownership structure between segments and venues.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:MarketSegment;
    rdfs:label "Market Segment Venue";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/TradingVenue/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:micEffectiveFrom a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "MIC Effective From, is the optional inclusive instant from which a MIC registry entry is effective per ISO 10383, used to record the entry lifecycle.";
    rdfs:label "MIC Effective From";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:micEffectiveTo a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "MIC Effective To, is the optional exclusive instant at which a MIC registry entry expires per ISO 10383, used to record the entry lifecycle.";
    rdfs:label "MIC Effective To";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:micEntryType a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "MIC Entry Type, is a closed classification attribute carried by one MIC registry entry, used to distinguish whether the entry is an operating-level or segment-level registry record.";
    rdfs:label "MIC Entry Type";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:MICEntryType.
fin-market-structure:micOperationalStatus a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "MIC Operational Status, is a closed classification attribute carried by a MIC registry entry, used to record the ISO 10383 lifecycle status (active, updated, expired) of the entry.";
    rdfs:label "MIC Operational Status";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:MICOperationalStatus.
fin-market-structure:micReplacedBy a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "MIC Replaced By, is a functional relation that associates a MIC registry entry with the MIC registry entry that replaces it when the entry has been superseded, used to model the ISO 10383 replacement chain as a logical reference.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:MICRegistryEntry;
    rdfs:label "MIC Replaced By";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/MICRegistryEntry/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:nonVenueContextConvention a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Non-Venue Context Convention, is a functional relation that associates a NonVenueMarketContext with its market-convention orientation, used to characterize the quoting orientation of a stable non-venue market context without carrying concrete currencies or execution semantics.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:NonVenueMarketContext;
    rdfs:label "Non-Venue Context Convention";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/MarketConvention/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:nonVenueContextProvider a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Non-Venue Context Provider, is a functional relation that associates a NonVenueMarketContext with the logical Party identity of its provider, used to characterize the data-source attribution of a stable non-venue context as a logical reference rather than an exact-version source contract.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:NonVenueMarketContext;
    rdfs:label "Non-Venue Context Provider";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Party/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:occurrenceCalendar a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Occurrence Calendar, is a functional relation that associates a session occurrence with the exact calendar version applied to it, used to characterize the calendar version on which an occurrence is based.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingSessionOccurrence;
    rdfs:label "Occurrence Calendar";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingCalendar.
fin-market-structure:occurrenceFacility a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Occurrence Facility, is a functional relation that associates a session occurrence with the exact TradingFacility version whose interval it controls, used to bind a tradable time window to a concrete venue version.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingSessionOccurrence;
    rdfs:label "Occurrence Facility";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingFacility.
fin-market-structure:occurrenceTemplate a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Occurrence Template, is a functional relation that associates a session occurrence with the exact template version that generated it, used to trace the template source of an occurrence.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingSessionOccurrence;
    rdfs:label "Occurrence Template";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingSessionTemplate.
fin-market-structure:operatedBy a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Operated By, is a functional relation that associates a TradingVenue with the logical Party identity that operates it, used to separate the market system/venue from its operator. The temporal validity and regulatory category of the operation are carried by VenueOperation; this relation is the logical-reference projection of the currently active operator.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingVenue;
    rdfs:label "Operated By";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Party/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:operatingMICEntry a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Operating MIC Entry, is a functional relation that associates a segment MIC entry with the exact operating MIC entry of its trading venue, used to characterize the correspondence between a segment and its venue's operating-level MIC.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:MICRegistryEntry;
    rdfs:label "Operating MIC Entry";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:MICRegistryEntry.
fin-market-structure:otcCounterpartyA a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "OTC Counterparty A, is a functional relation that associates an OTC trading context with the lexically first exact Party version in its optional counterparty pair, used to record one party of an over-the-counter execution in canonical form. Deprecated as of v1.1.0 with OTCTradingContext; counterparty semantics belong to orders-execution or post-trade-operations.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:OTCTradingContext;
    rdfs:label "OTC Counterparty A";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Party>.
fin-market-structure:otcCounterpartyB a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "OTC Counterparty B, is a functional relation that associates an OTC trading context with the lexically second exact Party version in its optional counterparty pair, used to record the other party of an over-the-counter execution in canonical form. This relation is deprecated as of v1.1.0 together with OTCTradingContext; counterparty semantics belong to orders-execution or post-trade-operations.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:OTCTradingContext;
    rdfs:label "OTC Counterparty B";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Party>.
fin-market-structure:otcQuoteCurrency a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "OTC Quote Currency, is a functional relation that associates an OTC trading context with its unique quote Currency logical identity, used to characterize the pricing currency of over-the-counter quotes. Deprecated as of v1.1.0 with OTCTradingContext; quote currency and quotation convention belong to instruments.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:OTCTradingContext;
    rdfs:label "OTC Quote Currency";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Currency/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:otcReportingFacility a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "OTC Reporting Facility, is a functional relation that associates an OTC trading context with its optional exact reporting-facility version, used to characterize the reporting venue on which an over-the-counter context relies. Deprecated as of v1.1.0 with OTCTradingContext; reporting obligation belongs to orders-execution or post-trade-operations.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:OTCTradingContext;
    rdfs:label "OTC Reporting Facility";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingFacility.
fin-market-structure:otcSettlementCurrency a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "OTC Settlement Currency, is a functional relation that associates an OTC trading context with its optional settlement Currency logical identity, used to characterize the settlement currency of over-the-counter executions. Deprecated as of v1.1.0 with OTCTradingContext; settlement currency belongs to instruments or post-trade-operations.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:OTCTradingContext;
    rdfs:label "OTC Settlement Currency";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Currency/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:otcSourceProvider a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "OTC Source Provider, is a functional relation that associates an OTC trading context with its exact source-provider Party version, used to characterize the data-source attribution of an over-the-counter context. Deprecated as of v1.1.0 with OTCTradingContext; provider attribution for the stable context is the logical nonVenueContextProvider, and the source contract moves to Layer 4.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:OTCTradingContext;
    rdfs:label "OTC Source Provider";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/Party>.
fin-market-structure:overrideAnnouncementOrder a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Override Announcement Order, is a non-negative integer recording the publication order of a TradingScheduleOverrideNotice within its calendar and facility scope, used to sequence notices by their announcement time.";
    rdfs:label "Override Announcement Order";
    rdfs:range xsd:integer.
fin-market-structure:overrideReplacementEndUtc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Override Replacement End UTC, is an optional exclusive replacement end instant supplied by a TradingScheduleOverrideNotice, used to override the closing instant of the affected scheduled occurrence when synthesizing the effective interval.";
    rdfs:label "Override Replacement End UTC";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:overrideReplacementStartUtc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Override Replacement Start UTC, is an optional inclusive replacement start instant supplied by a TradingScheduleOverrideNotice, used to override the opening instant of the affected scheduled occurrence when synthesizing the effective interval.";
    rdfs:label "Override Replacement Start UTC";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:overrideSupersessionOrder a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Override Supersession Order, is a non-negative integer recording the precedence of a TradingScheduleOverrideNotice when multiple notices affect the same occurrence, used together with the announcement order to synthesize a single final effective interval or cancellation.";
    rdfs:label "Override Supersession Order";
    rdfs:range xsd:integer.
fin-market-structure:providerContextId a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Provider Context Identifier, is a non-empty NFC business identifier scoped by one source provider and its immutable source contract, used to uniquely denote a context within an over-the-counter setting.";
    rdfs:label "Provider Context Identifier";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:recurrenceRule a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Recurrence Rule, is a bounded RFC 5545 RRULE-style recurrence expression that selects the business dates to which a session template applies, used to deterministically materialize occurrences under the calendar's IANA time zone. This attribute is the formal, materializable companion to the retained sessionRecurrence string.";
    rdfs:label "Recurrence Rule";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:registryAuthority a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Registry Authority, is a functional relation that associates a MIC registry entry with the logical identifier authority that maintains it, used to characterize the maintenance responsibility for MIC registry.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:MICRegistryEntry;
    rdfs:label "Registry Authority";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/IdentifierAuthority/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:registryFacility a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Registry Facility, is a functional relation that associates a MIC registry entry with the exact TradingFacility version it identifies, used to bind MIC registry facts to a concrete venue version.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:MICRegistryEntry;
    rdfs:label "Registry Facility";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingFacility.
fin-market-structure:registryMICValue a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Registry MIC Value, is a functional relation that associates a MIC registry entry with the unique four-character MIC logical identity it represents, used to link registry entries to their ISO 10383 MIC identifiers.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:MICRegistryEntry;
    rdfs:label "Registry MIC Value";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation/MICValue/LogicalIdentity>.
fin-market-structure:replacementSessionEndUtc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Replacement Session End UTC, is an optional exclusive replacement end instant supplied by an early closing exception, used to override the closing instant of the original session occurrence.";
    rdfs:label "Replacement Session End UTC";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:replacementSessionStartUtc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Replacement Session Start UTC, is an optional inclusive replacement start instant supplied by an early or late session exception, used to override the opening instant of the original session occurrence.";
    rdfs:label "Replacement Session Start UTC";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:scheduledTradingPhase a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Scheduled Trading Phase, is a closed classification attribute carried by a session template, used to distinguish preOpen, openingAuction, continuousTrading, closingAuction, postClose, maintenance, and reportingOnly phases of a trading session.";
    rdfs:label "Scheduled Trading Phase";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:ScheduledTradingPhase.
fin-market-structure:sessionBusinessDate a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Session Business Date, is the local calendar date to which a concrete trading-session occurrence belongs, used to assign an occurrence to a business day.";
    rdfs:label "Session Business Date";
    rdfs:range xsd:date.
fin-market-structure:sessionEndUtc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Session End UTC, is the exclusive UTC instant at which a concrete trading-session occurrence ends, used to bound the end of a trading session in absolute time.";
    rdfs:label "Session End UTC";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:sessionRecurrence a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Session Recurrence, is a deterministic recurrence expression, used to select the business dates to which a session template applies and bind a session specification to a concrete set of dates. Deprecated as of v1.1.0 in favor of the formal recurrenceRule attribute which is bounded and materializable; retained for compatibility.";
    rdfs:label "Session Recurrence";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:sessionStartUtc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Session Start UTC, is the inclusive UTC instant at which a concrete trading-session occurrence starts, used to bound the start of a trading session in absolute time.";
    rdfs:label "Session Start UTC";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:sourceContractDigest a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Source Contract Digest, is a lowercase SHA-256 digest, used to authenticate the exact bytes of the referenced source contract and verify that the contract content has not been tampered with. Deprecated as of v1.1.0 with OTCTradingContext; source-contract authentication belongs to Layer 4.";
    rdfs:label "Source Contract Digest";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:sourceContractRef a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Source Contract Reference, is the absolute IRI of the immutable provider schema or contract that defines the extraction of the provider context identifier, used to anchor the data-contract source of an over-the-counter context. Deprecated as of v1.1.0 with OTCTradingContext; the source contract belongs to Layer 4 SemanticMappingDefinition.";
    rdfs:label "Source Contract Reference";
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI.
fin-market-structure:templateCalendar a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Template Calendar, is a functional relation that associates a session template with the exact trading-calendar version it specializes, used to attach a session specification to a concrete calendar version.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingSessionTemplate;
    rdfs:label "Template Calendar";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:TradingCalendar.
fin-market-structure:tzdbRelease a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "IANA tzdb Release, is an optional versioned IANA time-zone database release identifier, used to pin the tzdb revision under which a trading calendar's local-clock sessions are materialized to UTC for deterministic replay.";
    rdfs:label "IANA tzdb Release";
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
fin-market-structure:venueCategory a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Venue Category, is a closed classification attribute carried by a VenueOperation, used to record the regulatory category of a trading venue (regulated market, multilateral trading facility, organized trading facility, or comparable category) as a temporal evidenced fact.";
    rdfs:label "Venue Category";
    rdfs:range fin-market-structure:VenueCategory.
fin-market-structure:venueOperationValidFrom a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Venue Operation Valid From, is the inclusive instant from which a VenueOperation is valid, used to bound the operator history of a trading venue.";
    rdfs:label "Venue Operation Valid From";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:venueOperationValidTo a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Venue Operation Valid To, is the exclusive instant at which a VenueOperation ends, used to bound the operator history of a trading venue.";
    rdfs:label "Venue Operation Valid To";
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp.
fin-market-structure:venueRegulatoryClassification a owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:comment "Venue Regulatory Classification, is a functional relation that associates a TradingVenue with its regulatory venue category (regulated market, multilateral trading facility, organized trading facility, or comparable category), used to model regulatory categorization as a temporal evidenced fact rather than a hardcoded global supertree. The temporal validity is carried by VenueOperation.";
    rdfs:domain fin-market-structure:TradingVenue;
    rdfs:label "Venue Regulatory Classification";
    rdfs:range <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure/VenueCategory/LogicalIdentity>.
